cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Belgrade green: the urban tree network as a graph and five ways to measure greenery"
abstract: >-
  Two small open-data studies of Belgrade, Serbia. Part 1 models the tree network of the city as a
  graph: tree patches from ESA WorldCover, least-cost links over a resistance surface with OSM roads
  and railways, the Probability of Connectivity, Equivalent Connected area and dPC (intra, flux,
  connector), build-over scenarios that rebuild the network, and circuit-theory pinch points. Part 2
  measures greenery in the ten urban parts of the settlement Beograd in five ways (Sentinel-2 NDVI,
  WorldCover tree cover, Meta/WRI 1 m canopy, street-level Green View Index from Mapillary, public
  green per resident) plus access to green space within 300 m, and compares their rankings.
